            <div xml:id="d416-a2-a15">

                <pb facs="0743" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg673"/>

                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">answer of the judge.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center">[Translation.]</p>
                <p>Those are not the facts, because the law regulating proceedings does not exact
                    the cross-examination to witnesses (law of the 5th of January, 1857), and also
                    because the defendant, to whom the case was transmitted for the term of three
                    days in order that he might suggest or cause to be done any convenient
                    proceedings in favor of the party in custody in the way of introducing evidence
                    or of talking testimony—he returned the same, stating that he had no further
                    proof to render.</p>
                <p>The trial of Captain Caleb was carried on by the court in conformity with the
                    laws of the country.</p>
                <p>(Not signed.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
